Verne is a GTK4 + libadwaita fork of Nemo, and stands entirely on the work of
two projects that came before it.

Nemo — the Cinnamon file manager, by Linux Mint
    https://github.com/linuxmint/nemo
    Nemo provides the file model, file operations, search, thumbnails,
    bookmarks, the extension API, the actions system and the settings schemas
    that Verne uses essentially unchanged.

GNOME Files (Nautilus) 3.4 — by the GNOME Project, Eazel, Inc. and Red Hat, Inc.
    https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/nautilus/tree/gnome-3-4
    Nemo started as a fork of Nautilus 3.4, so much of the code in this tree is
    ultimately Nautilus code.

GNOME Design Team — for the Adwaita icon theme and the visual language
    https://gitlab.gnome.org/Teams/Design

Thank you to everyone who contributed to any of the above.
